    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d576">

                <pb facs="0649" n="1327" xml:id="pg1327"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Dayton.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 430.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-11-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 14, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to the instruction of this
                    department to you relative to the exportation of tobacco belonging to foreign
                    governments in the United States, I enclose a copy of an Executive order of the
                    10th instant, by which you will perceive the condition upon which such
                    exportation has been licensed.</p>
                <p>It is expected that Mr. Mercier will soon adjust with me the particulars of the
                    regulations in regard to the tobacco belonging to France, the most if not the
                    whole of which is understood to be at Richmond.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> L. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dayton</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d576-a1.xml" xpointer="d576-a1"/>
            </div>
